// The throat is real geometry, not a painted disc: the water plane is projected in
// perspective, and because the surface is DEPRESSED the camera sits further above it than it
// does above the flat sea, so each pixel's ground distance is re-solved against its own height
// by fixed-point iteration. The funnel therefore bites a genuine hole in the perspective and
// its far wall compresses toward the horizon the way a real one does.
//
// Foam is not painted as spirals either. Every point is UNWOUND by the total angle its own
// radius has turned through, then read from a fixed field: since Omega(r) is far faster near
// the throat, the field is dragged into a spiral all by itself. Differential rotation draws it.
